d 'didc': module for difference-in-discontinuities designs
d
d Implements Picchetti, Pinto & Shinoki (2026, arXiv:2405.18531). In a
d regression-discontinuity design where a confounding policy is also assigned
d at the cutoff, the continuity assumption underlying standard RD fails.
d didc recovers the treatment effect by local polynomial estimation of the
d difference in outcomes over time (Delta Y) at the cutoff, following
d Calonico, Cattaneo & Titiunik (2014), and provides the validity tests and
d partial-identification bounds developed in the source paper:
d
d   didc          local polynomial DiDC estimator, bias-corrected robust
d                 inference, and a built-in check of the equivalence between
d                 "the RD of the differences" and "the difference of the RDs"
d   didc_test     (i) stacked-RD Wald test of time-invariant confounding, and
d                 (ii) bootstrap Kolmogorov-Smirnov test of time-invariant
d                 conditional means
d   didc_bounds   partially identified sets under bounded variation, with
d                 breakdown values
d
d Author: Haoyu Niu
d Distribution-Date: 20260930
d Requires: Stata version 17, rdrobust
d
